The starts on either side of the diagonal go to the state of the protein that starts higher; \((2, 2)\) lies exactly on the separatrix and converges to the saddle (B8). The four starts that have not settled at \(t = 30\) start close to the diagonal (\(|u_0 - v_0| = 0.2\) or \(0.3\)): they first slide in towards the saddle along its stable direction and then leave slowly, at rate \(0.19\). The two starts far from the diagonal settle by \(t = 30\).
