// I0 = 3  extinct 0.0369  se 0.0019  branching (1/3)^I0 = 0.0370



All three languages agree with \((1/3)^{I_0}\) within about 1 SE. The small differences from the branching-process value would come from \(S\) being slightly less than \(N\), which is negligible here. With \(I_0 = 10\) the extinction probability \(1.7 \times 10^{-5}\) is too small to estimate with 10 000 runs (expected 0.17 extinctions: the rare-event problem of Random numbers and Monte Carlo).

