The concentration peaks at 2.01 h at 3.34 mg/L. At \(k_a = k_e\) the formula is \(0/0\) = NaN, although the limit \(D k t e^{-kt}/V\) is perfectly finite (0.8187 and 1.7973 mg/L). Close to the diagonal the formula still works but subtracts two exponentials that agree to about 9 digits: catastrophic cancellation (Error, conditioning and stability), with a worst-case relative error of \(\varepsilon/10^{-9} \approx 2\times10^{-7}\). Here the result differs from the limit by \(1.6\times10^{-9}\), which is mostly the genuine effect of \(k_a - k_e = 10^{-9}\); at \(k_a - k_e = 10^{-13}\) the cancellation would leave only about 3 digits. The ODE form has no such problem; an optimiser that crosses \(k_a = k_e\) with the formula can hit NaN.
