Lie: the error halves with \(\Delta t\), order 1. Strang: the ratio grows from 2.7 to 3.3 per halving, approaching 4 (order 2) for small steps; at large steps the stiff diffusion modes and the boundary source reduce the order. (b) No source and uniform \(k\): the error is at rounding level for any \(\Delta t\), because the parts commute (B4(b)). (c) With the temperature step and no source: a real splitting error, order 1 for Lie. The exact digits of the rounding-level errors in (b) differ between R, Python and Rust (they use different expm algorithms).

