\(\Delta x = 1\) and \(0.5\) agree (47 and 46 spots: the noise is laid out differently on a different grid, so the exact count wanders by one). \(\Delta x = 2\) gives 63 spots: about 6 points per wavelength is too coarse (B6(b)). (b) The time step hardly matters for \(d = 20\) between 0.05 and 0.4. (c) With \(d = 5\) there is no Turing instability, and \(\Delta t = 0.1\) correctly stays uniform. \(\Delta t = 0.4\) makes \(|1 + \Delta t\lambda| = 1.039 &gt; 1\): Euler on the reaction amplifies the long waves (which implicit diffusion hardly damps) by 4 % per step, and a large, oscillating “pattern” appears. A pattern that exists only for some \(\Delta t\), or whose spacing follows \(\Delta x\), is a numerical artefact.

Background
The chamber. Oxygen in a 1 mm × 1 mm cell-laden gel, supplied through all four walls (concentration 1 = ambient) and consumed uniformly by the cells. The oxygen deficit \(u = 1 - c\) solves \(-\Delta u = \Phi\) with \(u = 0\) on the walls, \(\Phi = 12\). On an \(m \times m\) grid of interior points with spacing \(h = 1/(m+1)\), multiplied through by \(h^2\): \[4u_{ij} - u_{i-1,j} - u_{i+1,j} - u_{i,j-1} - u_{i,j+1} = \Phi h^2,\] a sparse SPD system \(A\mathbf{u} = \mathbf{b}\) with \(n = m^2\) unknowns and five non-zeros per row. The unknowns are numbered row by row: \(u_{ij}\) is entry \(i + m(j-1)\).
Facts used below:

Splitting. With \(A = M - N\): \(\mathbf{x}_{k+1} = \mathbf{x}_k + M^{-1}(\mathbf{b} - A\mathbf{x}_k)\). Jacobi: \(M = D\) (diagonal). Gauss–Seidel: \(M\) = lower triangle of \(A\) including the diagonal; in a sweep, each point uses the neighbours’ newest values.
Error and spectral radius. \(\mathbf{e}_{k+1} = T\mathbf{e}_k\) with \(T = I - M^{-1}A\). The iteration converges for every start if and only if \(\rho(T) = \max_i |\lambda_i(T)| &lt; 1\); the error shrinks by about \(\rho\) per step, so one digit takes \(\ln 10 / (-\ln \rho)\) steps.
On this grid: \(\rho_J = \cos \pi h\), \(\rho_{GS} = \cos^2 \pi h\), and \(\kappa(A) = \cot^2(\pi h/2) \approx 4/(\pi^2 h^2)\).
CG (SPD only) needs about \(\tfrac12\sqrt{\kappa}\,\ln(2/\text{tol})\) iterations at most; in practice the count grows like \(\sqrt{\kappa} \sim 1/h\).
Preconditioned CG replaces \(\mathbf{z} = \mathbf{r}\) by \(\mathbf{z} = M^{-1}\mathbf{r}\) with \(M \approx A\) SPD. Jacobi: \(M = D\). Incomplete Cholesky IC(0): \(M = LL^T\) where \(L\) has the pattern of the lower triangle of \(A\) (fill-in dropped).
GMRES finds the \(\mathbf{x}_k\) in the Krylov space \(\text{span}\{\mathbf{b}, A\mathbf{b}, \dots, A^{k-1}\mathbf{b}\}\) with the smallest residual; it works for nonsymmetric \(A\) but stores all \(k\) basis vectors.
Stopping: in this exercise every method stops when the relative residual \(\|\mathbf{b} - A\mathbf{x}\| / \|\mathbf{b}\| &lt; 10^{-6}\).

